{"authored" [{"question" "q-280321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,-3,2),$ $B(4,-1,5),$ $C(-2,0,1),$ and $D(3,-2,3).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "d80d4707806863fb023e367c55be7aa0e2d6c9aa9b9e2beb60ef368f3d1dec3a" "basis" 1756 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i-j+5k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j+3k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1)-2((-3)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3((-3)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(3+1)-2(-3+2)+3(-3-6) \\\\  & =12+2-27 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-13|=13.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "d80d4707806863fb023e367c55be7aa0e2d6c9aa9b9e2beb60ef368f3d1dec3a" "basis" 1756 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04d67fe3e6f61b1cf14d80c1722873bb5ae7c417577244f6ffc69393aebb4f2b" "basis" 1756 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "d80d4707806863fb023e367c55be7aa0e2d6c9aa9b9e2beb60ef368f3d1dec3a" "basis" 1756 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "d80d4707806863fb023e367c55be7aa0e2d6c9aa9b9e2beb60ef368f3d1dec3a" "basis" 1756 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-18266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors  $p=⟨0,-1,-{k}^{2}⟩,q=⟨2,4,8⟩$ and $r=⟨-1,-1,5⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-18266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -{k}^{2} \\\\ 2 & 4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|+(-{k}^{2})\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+(2\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 8)-{k}^{2}(2\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =18-2{k}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 18-2{k}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =9 \\\\ k & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-3$ or $k=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-18266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e612f42b0c9811dfa9a229c8b8ee5f5076056ca35f74326040da3324ce3fe84"} {"question" "q-18266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-18266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-1,k=1"] ["math" "k=-2,k=2"] ["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=-3,k=3"] ["math" "k=3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-18266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=-3,k=3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-73748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(2,-1,0)$, $B(-1,2,-1)$, $C(1,1,2)$, and $D(3,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-73748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j-k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =-i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-j+k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =i+k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-6+9+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|\\,5\\,|=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-73748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e612f42b0c9811dfa9a229c8b8ee5f5076056ca35f74326040da3324ce3fe84"} {"question" "q-73748" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-73748" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "17"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-73748" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-128461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨{k}^{2},7,4⟩,$ $b=⟨6,7,4⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,0,2⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-128461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2} & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}(7\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 4)-7(6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4)+4(6\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 7) \\\\  & =14{k}^{2}+0-84 \\\\  & =14{k}^{2}-84 \\\\  & =14({k}^{2}-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 14({k}^{2}-6) & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =6 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\sqrt{6}$ or $k=\\sqrt{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-128461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e612f42b0c9811dfa9a229c8b8ee5f5076056ca35f74326040da3324ce3fe84"} {"question" "q-128461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-128461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$k=-6$ or $k=6$"] ["text" "$k=-\\sqrt{3}$ or $k=\\sqrt{3}$"] ["text" "$k=-\\sqrt{6}$ only"] ["text" "$k=-\\sqrt{6}$ or $k=\\sqrt{6}$"] ["text" "$k=\\sqrt{6}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-128461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$k=-\\sqrt{6}$ or $k=\\sqrt{6}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-280314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(3,-2,1),$ $C(-1,4,-1),$ and $D(2,1,0).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-280314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =2i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+4j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-2i+4j+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =i+j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(8-1)+2(-4-1)+3(-2-4) \\\\  & =14-10-18 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-14|=14.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/state.json" "file_sha256" "f96648cd2f1dc88977df949a01852b8fa157ae067dc35f87b481256e70c7f4a0"} {"question" "q-280314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064170/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e612f42b0c9811dfa9a229c8b8ee5f5076056ca35f74326040da3324ce3fe84"} {"question" "q-280314" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/